{"public_message": "Quick record check, since the record is all we have. Everyone has now said they don't hold the money except Elena, and she hasn't had a chance to reply since we all asked her the same question. Elena, the floor is yours: why Jordan, and do you hold it, yes or no?

Sarah, two small corrections to your summary. Ben did answer your hypothetical: look reasonable, back the process, quietly amplify whatever suspicion already has momentum. Arvin also gave a denial, the brewery plan, and a pointed question to Elena. I'm guessing you were typing while those came in, which is probably what happened to Elena too.

That's my caution to the room. Six of us have now made the same point about one sentence that may just be a timing slip. By Ben's own playbook, the holder would love nothing more than to blend into a pile-on that's already rolling. So I'm keeping Elena as my lean until she answers, but I'm also watching who rides this wave hardest without adding anything new. If her answer is reasonable, who's everyone's second name? I'd like to hear that before we vote.", "private_message_to": null, "private_message": "", "notes_update": "Round 1 (mid): Everyone has now denied holding the money EXCEPT Elena, who hasn't replied to the pile-on yet. Six people (Ben, Arvin, Jordan, Gordon, Marcus, me) all hit Elena on the 'Jordan quiet' slip, which may just be a timing artifact. Sarah's summary was inaccurate: she said Ben hadn't answered and Arvin was a blank when both had. Likely timing too, but note it. Jordan repeated Sarah's 'comfortable, not clever' line nearly word for word, which is odd. Marcus piled on Elena hardest. Maya pushed back on Ben instead of joining the pile-on. Rules suggest a wrong vote eliminates no one, so accuracy matters more than self-protection. Lean: Elena pending her answer. Second looks: Sarah, Jordan, Marcus. Asked the room for second names.", "done": false}

